# Plan and documentation sync

The project plan is the source of truth for intent. Living documentation must stay synchronized whenever the plan changes.

## Source of truth

- Primary plan: `docs/plans/project-plan.md`
- Planning slices: `docs/plans/planning-phase.md`, `docs/plans/mvp-requirements.md`, `docs/plans/data-structure.md`
- Living docs that must track the plan:
  - `docs/PRODUCT.md`
  - `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
  - `docs/ROADMAP.md`
  - `docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md`
  - `README.md` (short summary + links only)
- Versioning policy for the plugin itself: `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc` (start at `0.0.1`; major digit only on official releases)
- Settings UI / Altlasten answers: `.cursor/rules/settings-ui-parity.mdc` (model lock ≠ GUI done; Knoten-/Attribut-Walk)
- While plan status is `planning`, also follow `.cursor/rules/planning-only.mdc` (docs/plans/rules only — no plugin implementation)

## Class diagram after structure changes

Whenever the **data structure** changes (objects, fields, or relations in `docs/plans/data-structure.md`):

1. Update the **Current class diagram** section in `docs/plans/data-structure.md` in the same change.
2. In the reply to the user, **always show the updated Mermaid class diagram** (not only a prose summary).
3. Keep the diagram aligned with agreed fields; mark tentative relations with `?` (for example Parameter ownership Q14).

## Required workflow

When you change goals, non-goals, phases, todos, status, architecture direction, or decisions in any file under `docs/plans/`:

1. Update `last_updated` (and plan version if the change is meaningful).
2. Update the affected living docs in the **same commit / PR**.
3. Ensure `docs/ROADMAP.md` phase tables match the plan phases and todo statuses.
4. Ensure `docs/PRODUCT.md` still matches in-scope / out-of-scope statements.
5. Ensure `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` still matches the planned technical shape (modules, APIs, data model).
6. Ensure `docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md` reflects newly decided or newly opened questions.
7. Refresh the README blurb if the one-line purpose, current mode, or current phase changed.

## Do not

- Do not leave the plan describing a different product than `docs/PRODUCT.md`.
- Do not mark plan todos completed without reflecting progress in `docs/ROADMAP.md`.
- Do not invent architecture in code without updating `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when it diverges from the plan.
- Do not create parallel “another plan” documents that compete with `docs/plans/project-plan.md` without linking them from the primary plan (`related_docs` / `related_plans`).
- Do not implement plugin code while `docs/plans/project-plan.md` status is `planning`.

## New slice plans

Additional files under `docs/plans/` are allowed for focused slices. Each must:

- Include frontmatter (`name`, `overview`, `status`, `todos` when useful).
- Be linked from `docs/plans/project-plan.md`.
- Trigger the same living-doc sync for any product, architecture, or roadmap impact.
